# Thread Sanitizer suppressions for scripts/weekly_sanitizer.py (TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<this file>).
#
# Every entry is a KNOWN finding with an open issue: a `# known:` line (code, issue,
# date, repro), `# reason:` lines, then exactly one suppression pattern. The runner
# refuses a pattern without that header (an unexplained suppression would hide a new
# finding), records each entry and its hit count in the run row, and the metrics card
# shows it as a grey "suppressed" count. Remove the entry when its issue closes.

# known: code=grdb-close-read-race issue=423 date=2026-11-08 repro=GRDBCloseTSanReproTests.readsInFlightDuringClose
# reason: GRDB 7.11.1 DatabasePool.close() writes readerPool = nil inside its barrier
# reason: (DatabasePool.swift:283) while read() reads it outside (:357). Real, inside GRDB;
# reason: needs a read starting while close runs (actor reentrancy in GRDBCatalogRepository).
# reason: Sequential awaited access then close does not fire. Not fixed in GRDB 7.12.0.
race:DatabasePool.close
